#pragma once

// Generated from aerora_credential_issuer.h.in by aerora/CMakeLists.txt. Do not edit.
//
// The Ed25519 public key of the party permitted to issue operator credentials for this build, as 64
// hex characters, or empty when no issuer is configured.
//
// Empty is the shipped default and it is load-bearing rather than a placeholder:
// AeroraEd25519Verifier::fromHex() returns null for it, so no verifier is installed, no credential
// is accepted, no identity is installed, and AeroraCommandAuthorizer::isFullyConfigured() stays
// false. A station built without this configured therefore enforces nothing and reports that it
// enforces nothing, which is the posture every document records today, reached by construction
// instead of by omission.
//
// A deployment that wants enforcement supplies its own key at configure time:
//
//   cmake -DAERORA_CREDENTIAL_ISSUER_PUBLIC_KEY=<64 hex characters> ...
//
// It is a build input rather than a file beside the credential deliberately. A public key an
// attacker can overwrite proves nothing: they would replace the key and the credential together and
// the signature would establish only that the two files agree. With no protected key store on any
// of the five platforms (D-DAT-05, F3.1-01), the binary is the one place this station holds that an
// actor who can write the save directory cannot also write. The cost is that rotating the issuer
// key needs a rebuild, which is accepted and recorded rather than hidden.
#define AERORA_CREDENTIAL_ISSUER_PUBLIC_KEY "@AERORA_CREDENTIAL_ISSUER_PUBLIC_KEY@"
